  "body": "Two proposals failed because they addressed a kernel that does not exist under the path they used. The rule as written names the kernel `conformance.kernel.grounding`: 'conformance.kernel.grounding: The harness's grounding verdict for a value, its cited span and the document, no relaxation, value-in-span checked: the input is one JSON object {\"value\", \"span\", \"document\"}; GROUNDED, SPAN_MISSING, SPAN_NOT_IN_DOCUMENT or VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN.' The source defines a private helper `def _grounding_kernel(text: str) -> str:`, but that is not the registered kernel identifier. The proposer misread the rule by using the function name `oracle._grounding_kernel` instead of the kernel name. The code part company with the proposer's path, not with the rule: the execution reports `MINI_OPEN_KERNEL_NOT_FOUND: 'oracle' has no '_grounding_kernel'`. Both dc50866bd0601688 and ec6f9b36cfa4fb89 failed for this reason. The proposer should next build a pair using the kernel `conformance.kernel.grounding` with an input object of the form `{\"value\": \"...\", \"span\": \"...\", \"document\": \"...\"}`. The proposal 446fc21b5b3ec099 passed and needs no critique.",
